{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100264","id":2227892217,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Eyu_5","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100264","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100264.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100264.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100264","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100264/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100264/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100264/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8e92728e954e1415422780b5e36297233ec19cfc","number":100264,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"servers/rendering: add new GLSL file format that is compatible with standard GLSL","user":{"login":"danderson","id":1918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson","html_url":"https://github.com/danderson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danderson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11274\r\n\r\nThe proposal has detailed justifications for the design, but TLDR: this change lets you write GLSL shaders where the Godot-specific hints are encoded as `#pragmas`, so that standard GLSL tools (IDE language servers, linters, glslang etc.) can parse the files and give a better development experience. The code supports both the new and existing file formats, so existing shaders keep working exactly as before.\r\n\r\nDetailed syntax and examples with more complex shaders is in the proposal, For a simple compute shader, the only change is the first 2 lines:\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\n#[compute]\r\n#version 450\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecomes:\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\n#version 450\r\n#pragma godot_shader_stages(compute)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI brought this to the rendering meeting earlier today and got :+1: on the concept, so here I am with code :)\r\n\r\nFor ease of reviewing, I split the change into multiple standalone commits. You can review each one separately, if you'd like smaller diffs with a single logical change in each. Godot compiles cleanly at every commit, so they can be merged as-is or I can squash them after review, your decision.\r\n\r\nAssuming this gets merged, I will send followup PRs to godot-docs and godot-example-projects to update the compute shader documentation to this format. I can also send followups to convert the internal shaders the renderers use, but I plan to check with the rendering folks again before I do that, to make sure I don't mess with other WIPs. It's not urgent to do, since the existing format will keep working.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","